WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
Unstable atoms give out three
kinds of nuclear radiation.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.390
One is stopped by a
single sheet of paper.

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.350
Another passes through paper,
but thin metal stops it.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.990
The third gets through
almost anything.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.750
It takes thick lead to cut it down.

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.870
Yet the one that paper stops
does the most damage along its

7
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.250
short path.

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.850
How can the weakest at getting
through be the most harmful?

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.930
In this mission, you'll meet
alpha, beta and gamma radiation,

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.410
and find out what each one is made of.

11
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.810
You'll compare how
far each one travels,

12
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:37.190
and discover what 'ionising' means.

13
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.070
Your mission: explain how the
radiation paper stops can be the

14
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.570
most harmful.
